A||||6||Jncomutt||Cradle, Engine, Or Tranny Mounts????||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||10-21-2001||08:31 PM||||How do I know when I need to replace my engine mounts, crade mounts or my tranny mount???<P>Whenever I go over speed bumps per se, I get a pretty good 'bang' or knock'(yes I go slow) Plus, if i'm just cruisin along say 40 in 4th gear (4 speed) without my foot on the gas, when I press it, even the slightest bit, It like 'bangs' again.  I'm thinking about replacing em all with Poly and I will be redoing my rear suspension as my winter project.  But I was just looking to see what I should look towards first, while I'm still driving everyday.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||10-21-2001||09:15 PM||||First thing to check is the dog bone. To check the quick way- park the car on some level ground engine off, put it in geat (4th) and the e brake off, rock the car back and forth and watch what moves and goes "clunk"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jncomutt||10-21-2001||10:58 PM||||Hey, never thought of that... THANKS!!<P>BTW: Just bought the ultimate dog bone from TFS hopin it wud matter, Nope.||||reg||1
